 "deviations": [
  "A71: the working point family is the FULL catalog arrangement's cell representatives reduced to inclusion-MAXIMAL membership patterns.  Sound because the (P2') load is monotone in the membership sets for z >= 0, so a dominated point's row is implied and the load maximum over the family is attained on maximal patterns; the cut loop and the validity check are therefore the same exact test on this family (no random subsampling, unlike A66's --fine_cap truncation).",
  "A71: cut-loop LPs are solved by HiGHS interior point with crossover OFF; every outer pass ends with a clean ipm solve (crossover=on) whose basic solution and row duals are what gets reported.",
  "A71: cell-representative point sets are HEURISTICALLY COMPLETE.  Each evaluated load is exact for its point, but maximality of the load over all of [0,s0]^2 rests on the representative construction (vertices + pairwise edge intersections nudged by 1e-05), not on a proof.",
  "core-free test uses the FULL unit pin (delta = 0), i.e. the strongest core; margin EPS_CORE = 1e-07 applied as |proj| >= (1+w)/2 - EPS_CORE (spec's literal reading)",
  "cutting-plane point set is augmented each round with arrangement-cell representatives (vertices + pairwise edge intersections of the CURRENT support squares, nudged by 1e-05 in the four diagonal directions); a plain 0.12/0.3 grid leaves Lmax >> 1 because the load is constant on arrangement cells that the grid never samples",
  "rows are deduplicated by their support set (not by point index), so the working point set may change between rounds without losing rows",
  "z has an upper bound 30 purely to keep intermediate LPs bounded; n_z_at_ub is reported"
 ],
